Confirmed and known issues

* **Storage Room ordinary farming is disabled** even though the room already has an enemy pool configured.
* **Legendary set bonuses are missing or not activating according to the approved 2-piece/3-piece rules.**
* Some older code still uses the previous **five-piece set logic** instead of the newer Legendary and Artifact thresholds.
* **Acceleration Shimmer skills advertise 40% stat bonuses but currently apply 25%.**
* Some Shimmer descriptions and actual runtime effects are still inconsistent.
* Equipment main-stat math is not fully aligned with the approved Equipment V2 rules.
* Early ATK/DEF equipment has been capable of granting extremely large flat bonuses, such as a Common weapon giving around +80 to +120 ATK to a character starting at 20 ATK.
* Because of that equipment scaling issue, a low-level player was able to defeat the fixed Level-8 Matron much earlier than intended.
* Inventory item-detail output can show mostly zeroes even when the item has a real percentage-based main stat.
* Equipment comparison/display still needs to show the actual effective stat changes rather than only the raw `Stats` structure.
* `RollLootInstance` needs continued review to ensure randomized rolls do not erase intentionally authored fixed bonuses or unique effects.
* The approved Legendary/Artifact set overhaul is not yet fully verified in live gameplay.
* Only eight distinct Artifacts have been naturally obtained so far, so several Artifact unique effects still lack live-play verification.
* Some Artifact mechanics may currently exist only as strings/placeholders or older simplified behavior and need deterministic testing.
* Combat still contains some older deterministic hit/status roll logic that should be replaced or fully standardized around seedable RNG.
* Consumable handling still needs a full audit for effect parsing, valid targeting, quantities, failed uses, and exact turn consumption.
* Large inventories make automated testing slower and can overwhelm the input driver, although the game itself did not hang in the reproduced case.
* Inventory locking/removal behavior should still be checked carefully when multiple copies of the same item exist.
* The exact Basic-enemy gear pity implementation still needs full live verification across long farming runs.
* Full rarity progression needs continued verification, especially Legendary and Artifact drops at high levels.
* Not every enemy skill/status combination has been exercised through live play yet.
* Not every individual Artifact trigger has been activated in a real naturally progressed run yet.
* The console presentation is still intentionally rough: no polished health bars, status icons, rarity colors, compact combat HUD, or improved spacing yet.
* The mystery/narrative side of the game is still mostly placeholder content compared with the much more developed combat/progression systems.
* Release/x86 configurations have not been as thoroughly runtime-tested as Debug x64.
* The newest endurance-run fixes and validation work may still be **uncommitted** because Codex hit its usage limit while staging/continuing the run.
